    {
      "text": "R4, verify-32 finding 3 (Unicode word boundaries): listed names and profile names match only as whole words in any script, including a decomposed accent (test line 1242 uses E+U+0301), Greek, Cyrillic and an Arabic-Indic digit. Non-letter neighbours (guillemets, en dash, NBSP) still separate words. HARDENER ADDITION: the one trading rule written as a bare regex (card_settlement, v1's synthetic wording) did not follow this rule: CAFÉACQUIRER SETTLEMENT was categorised revenue_card_settlement (reproduced before the fix). It is now a names list, so it uses the shared whole-word definition, with a new invariant test.",
      "proof_cmd": "python probe: classify('CAFÉACQUIRER SETTLEMENT') before the edit; pytest tests/test_rules_v2.py -k 'inside_a_longer_word_in_any_script or unicode_neighbours or profile_names_share or v1_acquirer_wording'",
      "proof_output": "before: 'CAFÉACQUIRER SETTLEMENT' (revenue_card_settlement, 'v2:card_settlement'); after: 10 passed + 3 passed (test_p_r4_v1_acquirer_wording_is_whole_words_in_any_script_too[ACQUIRER SETTLEMENT|PAYGATE PAYOUT|CARD SETTLEMENT])"
    },
    {
      "text": "D61: the category inside a bucket comes from the table's declared category_order (cash deposit, customer transfer, card settlement; returned payment, refund). The validator refuses a v2 table that does not order a bucket with two categories, lists one twice or names a non-category, and refuses category_order on a frozen table. Shuffling rules within each stage changes no category, reversal link or figure on whole statements (round-trip pass included), and the verify-32 round-trip repro keeps M2.",
      "proof_cmd": "pytest tests/test_rules_v2.py -k 'category_inside_a_bucket or declares_its_category_order or order_every_bucket or frozen_table_has_no or round_trip_statement_keeps or shuffling_rules_within_a_stage or shuffling_lists_within'",
      "proof_output": "13 passed; 3 passed"
    },
    {
      "text": "The four verify-27 repros are kept, and the verify-32 repros run end to end through cma run under CMA_RULESET=v2. Evidence lines carry the conflict form; only the genuine gateway payout is in M2; ambiguous and unmatched credits are in M16.",
      "proof_cmd": "pytest tests/test_rules_v2.py -k 'verify27 or verify32_repros'",
      "proof_output": "5 passed; 1 passed"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure modes / idempotency: re-categorising a statement gives the same category, rule id and reversal link on every line, with an override, profile and firm rule in play (recompute is idempotent). A malformed table is refused at load, naming the problem, so the categoriser never runs on a partial table. External-call timeouts, retries and dead letters: not applicable, because the categoriser makes no external call and has no queue (the evals test's subprocess has timeout=300).",
      "proof_cmd": "pytest tests/test_rules_v2.py -k 'idempotent or malformed_v2_rule or must_keep_its_stages'",
      "proof_output": "idempotent 1 passed; malformed-rule and stage tests pass within the 688 suite run"
    },
    {
      "text": "Data / migration: the change is additive. v2 is a new table, v1 stays frozen and pinned by hash, and v1 with frozen:false is refused. The evidence file gains a 'lines' key and keeps the old keys. It is reversible: switching CMA_RULESET back to v1 on a statement categorised under v2 equals a fresh v1 run, and pre-provenance (T01) and T02 checkpoints still resume with inferred v1 rule ids. P7: v2 changes only the listed lines and M1-M16 do not move on the committed corpus. Backfill: not applicable, because v2 is not the default and has written no signed pack; the card_settlement edit changes v2's hash only. PII: evidence lines hold id, category, rule_id and reverses only, never descriptions.",
      "proof_cmd": "pytest tests/test_rules_v2.py -k 'rollback_to_v1 or evidence_lines_carry_ids_only or p7_v2'; pytest tests/test_rules.py -k 't02_checkpoint or drafted_before_the_ruleset or switching_v1_frozen'; pytest tests/test_p7_history.py",
      "proof_output": "rollback 1 passed; evidence ids-only 1 passed; P7 passes in dual_run (83 passed); test_rules 3 passed; test_p7_history 5 passed"
    },
    {
      "text": "Security: there is no new entry point. The only new input is the CMA_RULESET value, which is checked against the RULESETS allow-list, and an unknown id is refused. Tables are validated at load: types, keys, and compile including OverflowError and RecursionError. Payer descriptions are only regex-searched, never interpolated into a command or query. No secrets are in the changed files. No new dependency: unicodedata is stdlib, and the only pyproject change since 43f3e57 is the pytest markers list.",
      "proof_cmd": "pytest tests/test_rules.py -k unknown_ruleset; rg -n -i 'api[_-]?key|secret|password|token' src/cma/rules src/cma/categorise.py tests/test_rules_v2.py; git diff 43f3e57 -- pyproject.toml",
      "proof_output": "1 passed; rg hits only REFERENCE_TOKEN (a regex name, not a secret); pyproject diff adds the markers list only"
    },
    {
