      "proof_cmd": "pytest tests/test_rules_v2.py -k 10000_lines",
      "proof_output": "1 passed in 0.69s (assert < 2.0s)"
    },
    {
      "text": "Observability: every evidence record names the ruleset id and hash and each line's rule_id, including the conflict form with its candidates, so a run proves which table and rule categorised each line. The evals summary names the ruleset. No remote alert, by design (design Observability: nothing leaves the machine); the failure that matters, a bad table, fails closed at load with a non-zero exit and no evidence written (test_cma_run_refuses_a_changed_v1_and_writes_no_evidence).",
      "proof_cmd": "pytest tests/test_rules_v2.py -k 'cma_run_under_v2_categorises_with_v2'; pytest tests/test_rules.py -k refuses_a_changed_v1",
      "proof_output": "both pass within the 688 suite run; record['ruleset'] == {'id': 'v2', 'sha256': ...}; per-line rule ids asserted"
    },
    {
